      "file": "tests/fixtures/luau-shield001/vulnerable/clamp-nan.server.luau",
      "fix": "The range check does not reject NaN: every comparison with NaN is false, so `if x <= 0 or x > max then return end` lets NaN through (and math.clamp/min/max return NaN for NaN). Add `if x ~= x then return end`. Let the server decide amounts (look prices and rewards up in a server table by an allow-listed id). If a number must come from the client, check `typeof(x) == \"number\"`, reject NaN (`x ~= x`) and check both bounds before using it. Never use client data as a DataStore key.",
      "flow": [
        {
          "column": 52,
          "file": "tests/fixtures/luau-shield001/vulnerable/clamp-nan.server.luau",
          "line": 23,
          "note": "`requested` (parameter #2) of the `Withdraw.OnServerInvoke` handler is sent by the client (the type annotation `unknown` is not checked at runtime)"
        },
        {
          "column": 8,
          "file": "tests/fixtures/luau-shield001/vulnerable/clamp-nan.server.luau",
          "line": 29,
          "note": "assigned to `amount`"
        },
        {
          "column": 2,
          "file": "tests/fixtures/luau-shield001/vulnerable/clamp-nan.server.luau",
          "line": 30,
          "note": "`amount` (client-controlled, from `requested`) is subtracted from `account.BankBalance`"
        }
      ],
      "help_uri": "https://github.com/Topogamer0/luau-shield/blob/main/docs/rules/luau-shield001.md",
      "line": 30,
      "message": "`amount` (client-controlled, from `requested`) is subtracted from `account.BankBalance`",
      "rule": "luau-shield001",
      "severity": "high",
      "slug": "untrusted-economy-write",
      "snippet": "\taccount.BankBalance -= amount -- expect: luau-shield001",
      "title": "Client-controlled value written to currency, stats or saved data",
      "why": "Exploiters can fire any remote with any arguments. If the server adds a client-supplied amount to a currency, saves a client-supplied table or lets the client pick the DataStore key, an exploiter can give themselves unlimited currency, corrupt other players' data or poison saves with NaN/huge values. Luau type annotations are erased at runtime: they do not validate anything."
    },
